course: dictionary
lesson: 2135
title: Cooling: one word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cooling comes from the word cool, and it can work as more than one kind of word. As a verb, it means becoming cooler or making something cooler. «A burn is cooled under cool running water for 20 minutes» tells you that the water makes the burn cooler.
explain: As a describing word, cooling tells you what something does. «Use the cooling lotion an adult gives you» means the lotion makes your skin feel cooler. Try it: swap in "the lotion that cools" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: As a noun, cooling is the process of lowering temperature, or a system that does it. «In a home most energy is used for heating, cooling and hot water» means the things that keep a home at the right temperature. Use the sentence clues to decide which job the word is doing.
fact: Cooling means becoming cooler, or making something cooler.
fact: As a describing word, cooling tells you something makes you feel cooler, like a cooling lotion.
fact: As a noun, cooling is the process of lowering temperature, or a system that does it.
fact: «Cooling stops the burn going deeper», so a burn is cooled under running water for 20 minutes.
fact: «Water puts out fires mainly by cooling», because it soaks up a lot of heat as it turns to steam.
exercise: «A burn is cooled under cool running water for 20 minutes.» What does cooled mean here? | *Made cooler | Made bigger | Made louder | Made wet and sticky
exercise: «Use the cooling lotion an adult gives you.» What does cooling describe? | A lotion for sleeping in | *A lotion that makes your skin feel cooler | A lotion that is very hot | A lotion that is a type of food
exercise: «Lava cools to make rock.» What does cools mean here? | *Becomes cooler until it is solid | Turns into water | Becomes hotter | Grows bigger and taller
test:
«Water puts out fires mainly by cooling.» What is the main way water puts out fires? | *By lowering the heat | By making the fire louder | By making the fire spread faster | By turning the fire blue
«Cooling stops the burn going deeper.» Why is cooling a burn helpful? | *It stops the heat damaging more skin | It makes the burn bigger | It makes the burn hotter | It turns the burn into steam
exam:
In «a home's cooling system», what does cooling mean? | A cooling breeze on a hot summer day | *The process or system that lowers the temperature | Something that is very old | A slow walk around the house
